Photograph input
: A JPEG, PNG, HEIC/HEIF, AVIF, TIFF, or WebP image containing the complete
  puzzle and reference grid.

Puzzle TOML
: A deterministic representation of the grid, blocks, numbered symbols,
  supplied clues, OCR uncertainties, and optional answer grid.

Solved photograph
: By default, `--image` writes `<input-stem>_solved.<input-format>` beside the
  source photograph. Existing files are protected unless `--force` is used.

Temporary working files
: OCR crops, rectified grids, and uploaded web photographs are created in a
  temporary directory and discarded when the command or request finishes.

`pyproject.toml`
: Project metadata, dependencies, tool configuration, and web-service defaults.
